    "related_formalizations": [
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/math-comp/fourcolor",
        "note": "The Coq/Rocq formal proof by Georges Gonthier et al. (Microsoft Research and Inria, CeCILL-B; now maintained as coq-community/fourcolor), ported from commit c1d6b1cd5288bea4b067aac13cdde3c18dffe018. Definitions, statements, proof structure and the combinatorial data are translated; the tree-based reducibility decision procedure is replaced by a new kernel-checkable engine (see fidelity.divergences).",
        "relationship": "adapts"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/corun1024/4ct",
        "note": "Chris Emery's Lean 4 formalization of the same statement, public before this one: complete, also following Gonthier and Werner's proof, and also written mostly by AI (Claude Fable 5.1). Its reducibility certificates are produced before the Lean build by C and Python programs and are not in its repository (the kernel checks them). Here every file of the proof is Lean source in the repository, and the certificates are computed by Lean code during the build, so the Lean toolchain alone builds and checks the proof. README.md (\"Other formalizations\") lists the other differences.",
        "relationship": "independent"
